.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-GET-BUCKET 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket \- show one bucket's definition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm get-bucket
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I NAME\fR|\fIERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one bucket as JSON: its ERN, the account and namespace it belongs
to, its region, size and object count, whether its objects are
encrypted and under which key, its tags, and when it was created and
last changed.
.PP
This is the same description
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-buckets (1)
gives of each of its own, for a single bucket asked for by name. They
share one representation on purpose, so that a field added to a listing
is in this too rather than the two drifting apart.
.PP
For a single number there are narrower commands that cost less:
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-size (1)
for the byte total and
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-object-count (1)
for the stored object count.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fINAME\fR|\fIERN\fR
The bucket. Required. A name is resolved in your session's account and
namespace \- which is where
.BR euclid-cli-esm-create-bucket (1)
would have put it \- so it means your bucket of that name and cannot
reach another account's bucket called the same thing. A full ERN names
one bucket in the installation and is what reaches another namespace's;
see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The bucket is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no such
bucket exists, or the session's grants do not cover it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
By name, in your own namespace:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm get-bucket --bucket file-delivery
.fi
.RE
.PP
By ERN, which reaches any namespace you are granted:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm get-bucket \\
    --bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:bucket:file-delivery
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-buckets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-ern (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-size (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-object-count (1)
